    "title": "New AEW World Trios Champions Crowned - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Ryan Clark ,\n1 hours ago\nThe AEW World Trios Championships have new owners following a major title change at AEW Grand Slam: Mexico.\nDuring Wednesday night’s special edition of AEW Dynamite from Arena México, Adam Page and Brodido dethroned The Demand to capture the AEW World Trios Titles.\nREAD MORE: Samoa Joe – ‘The Whole ‘Locker-Room Leader’ Label Is Weird’\nREAD MORE: MJF Returns At AEW Grand Slam: Mexico\nThe decisive moment came when Page hit Toa Liona with a Buckshot Lariat as Brodido launched him backward with a bridging German suplex, keeping Liona’s shoulders on the mat long enough for the referee to count three.\nThe loss brings The Demand’s reign to an abrupt end after just one week as champions. The trio had won the titles on the July 29 episode of Dynamite by defeating The Conglomeration — Kyle O’Reilly, Orange Cassidy, and Roderick Strong — but were unable to make a successful title defense before dropping the belts.\nNOTE: If you have any news tips or podcast recaps that you’d like to send in for us to post (full credit will be given to you), please email me at RClarkPWS@Yahoo.com .\n1",
    "summary": "During Wednesday night’s special edition of AEW Dynamite from Arena México, Adam Page and Brodido dethroned The Demand to capture the AEW World Trios Titles. READ MORE: Samoa Joe – ‘The Whole ‘Locker-Room Leader’ Label Is Weird’ READ MORE: MJF Returns At AEW Grand Slam: Mexico The decisive moment came when Page hit Toa Liona with a Buckshot Lariat as Brodido launched him backward with a bridging German suplex, keeping Liona’s shoulders on the mat long enough for the referee to count three. The loss brings The Demand’s reign to an abrupt end after just one week as champions.",
